ADR-034 fast-fail evidence: `tbard --service` unprivileged → exit 1 in ~10ms.

Verbatim capture (cargo test --test service_root_guard -- --nocapture):
  ok: `tbard --service` unprivileged fast-failed in 10.2576ms with the
  typed ServiceRequiresRoot error (exit 1) per ADR-034
  test test_service_unprivileged_fast_fails ... ok

The fast-fail is the regression target for NF-A2:
- Pre-ADR-034 (and pre-ADR-033): ~30min (NF-A1 nested retry) before
  exit 1.
- Post-ADR-033, pre-ADR-034: ~90s (flattened retry budget) before
  exit 1.
- Post-ADR-034: ~10ms (hard root guard at entry, BEFORE any scanning or
  retry).

The `Restart=on-failure` spin-storm is impossible: the daemon exits
fast with a greppable typed error ("service mode requires root
(euid=1000); start as root or via the systemd unit (tbard.service) —
exit 1"). The operator sees the error in the journal immediately.

The test runs as the current (unprivileged, uid 1000) user. If run as
root (e.g. under sudo), it skips truthfully — the fast-fail is
unprivileged-only. The real privdrop path (root → nobody) remains
QA/Stage-3 acceptance (unchanged).